{"id":"word:hebrew:H68","type":"word","title":"אֶבֶן","subtitle":"H68 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"a stone","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אֶבֶן (H68) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-f.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 273 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אֶבֶן (ʼeben) means a stone First listed occurrence: 1Chr 12 2."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אֶבֶן","transliteration":"ʼeben","pronunciation":"eh'-ben","strong":"H68","lemmaId":"hebrew:H68","partOfSpeech":"n-f","forms":["אֶ֣בֶן","אַבְנֵי","אֶ֖בֶן","אֲבָנִ֣ים","אַבְנֵ֣י"],"morphs":[["HNcfsa",52],["HNcfpa",41],["HNcfpc",29],["HTd/Ncfpa",20],["HC/Ncfsa",20],["HTd/Ncfsa",20],["HRd/Ncfpa",19],["HNcfsc",13],["HC/Ncfpc",10],["HRd/Ncfsa",7]]},"definitions":{"short":"a stone","usage":"carbuncle, mason, plummet, (chalk-, hail-, head-, sling-) stone(-ny), (divers) weight(-s).","full":"H68. eben אֶ֫בֶן 274 noun feminine Gen 29:2 ( masculine 1Sam 17:40 ?) stone (Assyrian abnu , = the sharp, projecting ? see Dl W, Pr 107 ; Phoenician אבן ; Aramaic אֶבֶן , ; Ethiopic Sabean [ ם ] אבנ DHM ZMG 1883, 341 ) — ׳א absolute Gen 28:22 +; אָ֑בֶן 11:3 +; construct 49:24 +; suffix אַבְנוֺ 2Kin 3:25 ; אֲבָנִים Gen 31:46 +, etc.; — a stone (large or small). 1 in natural state, used as pillow Gen 28:11 , 18 (E); seat Exod 17:12 (E); cover of well Gen 29:2-3 ,(twice in verse); 29:8 , 10 (J); causing one to stumble Isa 8:14 ; marring good ground 2Kin 3:19 , 25 ; hand-missle Exod 21:18 (JE) Num 35:17 , 23 (P) 2Sam 16:6 , 13 , especially in judicial stoning, with verb רָגַם Lev 20:2 , 27 ; 24:23 ; Num 14:10 ; 15:35-36 , Josh 7:25 a (all P), so also Deut 21:21 ; 2Chr 24:21 ; Ezek 16:40 ; 23:47 ; compare 1Kin 12:18 2Chr 10:18 ; with verb סָקַל Deut 13:11 ; 17:5 ; 22:21 , 24 ; 1Kin 21:13 ; also Josh 7:25 b (J E or D); sling-stones Judg 20:16 ; 1Sam 17:40 , 49 (twice in verse); 17:50 ; 2Chr 26:14 ; hurled by engines 26:15 ; set up for inscribing law Deut 27:2 , 4 , 8 ; Josh 8:32 (all D); as memorial 4:3 , 5 , 6 , 7 , 8 , 9 , 20 , 21 (J E D) 1Sam 7:12 ; as sacred pillar ( מַצֵּבָה ) Gen 28:18 ; 35:14 (anointed with oil), 28:22 (= בֵּיתאֵל ) compare יִשְׂרָאֵל א ׳(רֹעֶה) 49:24 (see Di); as witness 31:45 compare Josh 24:26-27 , (all J E); plural gathered into heap ( גַּל ) over dead, 7:26 (see Di) 8:29 ; compare 10:18 , 27 (JE) 2Sam 18:17 ; גַּל on which meal was eaten, in a compact Gen 31:46 (twice in verse) (JE); built into altar Exod 20:25 ; Deut 27:5-6 , (J E D) Josh 8:31 ; 1Kin 18:31-32 , 38 ; compare 2Kin 23:15 ᵐ5 Klo (for הבמה ); of figured stone (forbidden) ׳א מַשְׂכִּית Lev 26:1 (H) ; ׳א גדולה where ark rested 1Sam 6:14-15 , also 6:18 ( ᵑ0 אבל q. v.); (see for other note-worthy stones 9 below 2 stone, as material , of tablets Exod 24:12 ; 31:18 ; 34:1 (plural) 34:4 ; 34:4 (JE) Deut 4:13 ; 5:19 ; 9:9-10 , 11 ; 10:1 , 3 ; of vessels, hence probably Exod 7:19 (P; ׳א = vessels of stone || עצים ) see Di; idols (|| עץ ) Deut 4:28 ; 28:36 , 64 ; 29:16 ; 2Kin 19:18 = Isa 37:19 ; also Jer 3:9 ; Ezek 20:32 ; pavement 2Kin 16:17 ; edifice 1Kin 6:7 compare Gen 11:3 ; also 2Sam 5:11 ; 2Kin 12:13 ; 1Chr 22:15 ; often plural of (worked) stones Lev 14:40 , 42 (twice in verse); 14:43 , 45 (P; in wall of house) 2Kin 22:6 +, compare of city-wall Nehemiah 3:35; of (ruined) city 1Kin 15:22 ; Nehemiah 3:34; tomb Isa 14:19 ; יְקָרוֺת אֲבָנִים (costly building-stones) 1 Kings 5:31; 1Kin 7:9-10 , 11 (see also below 3 ); שַׁיִשׁ אַבְנֵיֿ = marble (see ᵐ5 ) 1Chr 29:2 ; גָזִית אַבְנֵי = hewn stones 1 Kings 5:31; 22:2 ; Ezek 40:42 (for altar-tables), — compare גָּזִית ; ׳א מַחְצֵב 2Kin 12:13 ; 22:6 ; 2Chr 34:11 ; foundation-stone, corner-stone Isa 28:16 ; Jer 51:26 ; Job 38:6 ; Psa 118:22 ; cap-stone, completing the building, ׳הָא הָרִאשֹׁנָה Zech 4:7 (but see מִּנָּה רֹאשׁ Psa 118:22 as above), Zech 3:9 upon one stone seven eyes , probably refers to this cap- or head-stone; the eyes are symbol of God's watchfulness; perhaps explaining cup-stones found in Orient, see Guthe ZPV 1890, 129 ; stone-cutters א ׳חָרָשֵׁי 2Sam 5:11 ; 1Chr 22:15 ; הָא ׳חֹצְבֵי 2Kin 12:13 compare 1Chr 22:2 . 3 precious stones , Generally with modifying word ׳א יְקָרָה collective 2Sam 12:30 ; 1Kin 10:2 + often (see 2 ); ׳א הַשֹּׁהַם Gen 2:12 (J) compare Exod 25:7 ; 28:9 ; 35:9 , 27 ; 39:6 (P) 1Chr 29:2 ; ׳א מִלֻּאִים Exod 25:7 ; 35:9 , 27 compare 1Chr 29:2 ; ׳א סַמִּיר Ezek 1:26 ; 10:1 ; אֶקְדָּח אַבְנֵי Isa 54:12 ; ׳א חֵפֶץ ib. ; וְרִקְמָה פוּח אַבְנֵי 1Chr 29:2 ; ׳א חֵן Prov 17:8 ; on אֵשׁ אַבְנֵי ( stones of fire ) Ezek 28:14 , 16 as precious stones = Assyrian aban išâti (?) see Dl Pa 118 & W 40 ; but Sm and others thunderbolts ; also without distinctive modifier Exod 25:7 ; 35:9 ; א ׳חָרַשׁ engraver in stone 28:11 ; compare 31:5 ; 35:33 (P). 4 stones containing metal , = ore , Deut 8:9 (see Di) Job 28:2 compare 28:3 . 5 a weight , originally stone (see Prov 27:3 compare English weight stone = 14 lb) אַבְנֵיכִֿיס 16:11 (compare Assyrian Dl W 38 ); ׳א הַמֶּלֶח 2Sam 14:26 (i.e. accusative to royal standard; compare COT Gen 23:16 ); ׳א ׳וָא Deut 25:13 ; Prov 20:10 , 23 (i.e. different weights, for dishonest use); מִרְמָה אַבְנֵי כִּיס Micah 6:11 ; just weights אַבְנֵיצֶֿדֶק Lev 19:36 ; ׳א שְׁלֵמָה Prov 11:1 ; hence also heavy mass of metal (lead) Zech 5:8 . 6 plummet Isa 34:11 ( stones of devastation , or emptiness , compare on sense 2Kin 21:13 ; Amos 7:7-8 ,); also made of metal ׳הא הַבְּדִּיל Zech 4:10 (conversely plummet from plumbum ). 7 objects like stones; particle hail , explicitly, הַבָּרָד אַבְנֵי Josh 10:11 compare Isa 30:30 ; ׳א אֶלְגָּבִישׁ Ezek 13:11 , 18 ; 38:22 ; but also גְּדֹלוֺת אֲבָנִים Josh 10:11 (E) (compare Assyrian Dl W 38 ); lime-stones אַבְנֵיגִֿר Isa 27:9 . 8 in simile (mostly poetry) of sinking in water Exod 15:5 = Neh 9:11 ; motionlessness Exod 15:16 ; strength Job 6:12 ; firmness 41:16 ; solidity (of ice) 38:30 ; in prose, of commonness 1Kin 10:27 ; 2Chr 1:15 ; also metaphor of one in fear 1Sam 25:37 (i.e. 653petrified with terror, compare Exod 15:16 above); הָא ׳לֵב = perverse, hard heart Ezek 11:19 ; 36:26 ; אַבְנֵינֵֿזֶר Zech 9:16 (of ransomed Israel) — ׳א personified Hab 2:11 compare 2:19 ; compare Ezek 13:11 (see 7 above) 9 In topographic terms (nearly = proper name); בֹּהַן אֶבֶן Josh 15:6 ; 18:17 ; ׳א הָעֶזֶר 1Sam 5:1 ; compare 7:12 , also 4:1 (We Dr); הָאָ֑זֶל ׳הָא 20:19 , read הַלָּאז הָאַרְגָּב see ᵐ5 here & 20:41 (We Dr Klo); ׳א הַזֹּחֶלֶת 1Kin 1:9 (where We Skizzen III, 171 compare Arabic Zuhal = Saturn). אַרְגָּב noun masculine heap, mound (probably); — so read 1Sam 20:19 (for אבן ), 20:41 (for ננב ), ᵐ5 ( αρ σαβ, ερσαβ ), Th We Klo Dr Kit Bu HPS. אֶ֫בֶן noun feminine Dan 2:34 stone (Biblical Hebrew id .); — absolute ׳א 2:34 +; emphatic אַבְנָא 2:35 ; &#8212; 1 a (the) stone Dan 2:34-35 , 45 ; 6:18 . 2 stone , material of idols Dan 5:4 , 23 ; of buildings Ezra 5:8 ; 6:4 .","rootNote":"from the root of 1129 through the meaning to build ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 12 2","keyReferences":["1Chr 12 2","1Chr 20 2","1Chr 22 2","1Chr 22 14","1Chr 22 15","1Chr 29 2","1Chr 29 2","1Chr 29 2"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":273,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 12 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":12,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"בָּֽ/אֲבָנִ֔ים","source":"hebrew","morph":"HRd/Ncfpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 20 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":20,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֶ֣בֶן","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfsa"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אַבְנֵ֣י","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNcfpc"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 14","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/אֲבָנִים֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Ncfpa"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 15","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֶ